analysisWe need to produce assert statement for the comment.

We have method set(int index, E element). It checks element index, then modifies node at index to new element, returns old value.

Comment: 
"@@@ If the index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the initial size of the list), then for every index from 0 up to but not including the specified index, either both the current and the old value at that index are null, or the current value at that index is equal to the old value at that index."

Interpretation: For all i such that 0 <= i < index, we have that after operation, this.get(i) equals old value at that index, i.e., \old(this.get(i)). Also mention null case: either both are null or they are equal. That's essentially same as equality (since null equals null). So we can assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) . But need to handle null: use (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || (this.get(i) != null && this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) . However typical spec uses .equals which would throw NPE if null. In examples they used this.query(i).equals(\old(this.query(i))) assuming query returns object and equals works (maybe they rely on JML's .equals handling null?). In earlier example they used .equals without null check. So we can use this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))). But need to ensure index valid: condition index >=0 && index < \old(this.size()). The comment says "index is valid (greater than or equal to 0 and less than the initial size of the list)". So we need to assert that if that condition holds, then the forall holds. So we can write: assert (index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i)));

We need to refer to size method: this.size() returns current size after modification, but we need initial size before set. Since set does not change size, size unchanged, so old size equals current size. But to be precise we can use \old(this.size()).

Thus final assert statement:

